# SFT execution status v0.97

2026-09-17. Local diagnosis of the consumed native qualification failure is
complete. Its exact historical cause remains unproven; no native attempt was
rerun. Source/Spark CI success recorded in v0.96 is unchanged.

## What the local check established

The old harness labels its whole setup block `source_admission`. Nine distinct
synthetic failures in that block produce the same `fixture_failed` report.
Those include source/helper loading, subreaper setup, temporary-directory setup,
disk-query failure and insufficient disk space.

In particular, free disk one byte below the unchanged 16 GiB floor reproduces
the exact retained harness-output SHA-256. This is a demonstrated possible
cause, **not proof that the old host lacked disk space**: no disk count or finer
setup stage was retained. The old workflow acquired its software archive before
checking this disk floor.

The actual 78-file source closure and both helper loaders passed inert local
checks with native-library/process/socket/fork operations denied. No deterministic
loader defect was found. No Linux `prctl` or native harness execution occurred.

## Verification and preservation

- 14 new local synthetic tests plus the 21 unchanged harness tests passed in
  both orders on Python 3.11.15 and 3.13.7: four runs, 140 test executions,
  zero skips. This is source/synthetic evidence, not Linux qualification.
- Ruff 0.15.1 passed. Review caught two test-module namespace isolation issues;
  both were fixed and covered by restoration regressions before final runs.
- The old harness, supervisor, acquisition helper, verifier, tests, execution
  plan and four retained aggregates still match their previous hashes.
- No tracked source, workflow, threshold or execution permission changed.
  No network, GitHub push, Docker operation, GPU or real model/data access.

New local files: the localization regression test, its aggregate evidence and
this status note. They have not been published.

## Next needed step

Prepare and separately authorize a small fresh CPU-only Linux preflight with
fixed setup-substage codes and a disk-capacity aggregate, **before** any software
image acquisition. It needs no GPU, model or dataset. It must preserve the
16 GiB floor, report acquisition headroom, and must not invoke the full prepared
pipeline or reuse the consumed native attempt. Current-host observations would
not retroactively prove what happened on the old disposable host.

Gate 5 remains incomplete. Full native qualification and real SFT training are
not authorized or claimed by this diagnostic.

Evidence: `evidence/lumi-4b-sft-prepared-source-localization-v0.1.json`.
